  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220A={63}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({63}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{3x+2}{3x} \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({63}^{\u2218}) & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({63}^{\u2218})-3x & =2 \\\\ 3x(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({63}^{\u2218})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{3(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({63}^{\u2218})-1)} \\\\ x & =0.692\\,5\u2026\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x+2=3(0.692\\,5\u2026)+2=4.077\\,6\u2026, \\\\ AC & =3x=3(0.692\\,5\u2026)=2.077\\,6\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(2.077\\,6\u2026)(4.077\\,6\u2026) \\\\  & =4.236\\,0\u2026 \\\\  & \u22484.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
